    label "public abstract void enforceCallingOrSelfPermission(@NonNull @PermissionName String permission, @Nullable String message)"
    type "method"
    comment "&#10;     * If neither you nor the calling process of an IPC you are&#10;     * handling has been granted a particular permission, throw a&#10;     * {@link SecurityException}.  This is the same as {@link&#10;     * #enforceCallingPermission}, except it grants your own&#10;     * permissions if you are not currently processing an IPC.  Use&#10;     * with care!&#10;     *&#10;     * @param permission The name of the permission being checked.&#10;     * @param message A message to include in the exception if it is thrown.&#10;     *&#10;     * @see #checkCallingOrSelfPermission(String)&#10;     "
  ]
